            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_2",
            "review_title": "Review at Com Tam Bai Rac",
            "review_text": "Alex C\nMui Ne, Vietnam\n183 contributions\n0\nHidden gem in the market\nSep 2017 • Couples\nThe stall is open usually at night, and they are situated in the Xom Chieu Market, District 4. It's not easy to find it on the map, but you can ask the locals where's the \"Cơm Tấm Bãi Rác\". The term is very famous, and most of locals know it. Because of the bad environment, the stall is named after that. However, the outstanding rice with ribs, or sunny side-ip eggs make us forgetting the surrounding area. The price is quite high compared to other broken price stalls. But it worth every penny, and I hope that the tourist visit this place every time they come to HCM city, it's a signature of Vietnamese street food. 5 star for this place\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten October 1, 2017",
