            "review_id": "REV_12604057_p1_3",
            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_3",
            "review_title": "Review at Com Tam Bai Rac",
            "review_text": "Simon P\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam\n111 contributions\n0\nThe Best Broken Rice - local family styled!\nJun 2017 • Solo\nLocated at the back of Xom Chiu Market and only open when the Market closes (6-7pm) so the area is a lil bit messy with all the \"leftovers\". Hence the name \"Bai Rac\", and its is NOT an actually \"waste-dumping spot\". \nI know its not the best location for some, but for me the quality can make up for anything! \nI still remember the first time I came, I was overwhelmed by the environment, but after eating the most delicious broken rice with well-seasoned Ba Rọi (grilled pork belly) and a perfectly cooked sunny side-up egg (duck egg, crips egg white and runny egg york). It is so TASTY, that mouth-watering experience keep me coming back for more every now and then. \nUsually, people would order Com Suon Trung Opla (grilled pork chop + egg) but I highly you try the Ba Rọi one or Pork Ribs (grilled pork ribs).\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten June 28, 2017",
